Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0030 (touches nvidia/dspark.py
and nvidia/ops/markov_cache.py). VLLM_DSPARK_MARKOV_FUSED=1 (default off; needs VLLM_DSPARK_LOCAL_ARGMAX=1 and the
Markov cache): each of the five Markov steps of DSpark's local draft argmax runs the bias (the cached row of the
previous token, or markov_w2 @ markov_embed for an uncached one), its add to the shard's base logits and the shard's
max in two launches: a (max, first argmax) per 128 columns, then a per-row reduction to the (value, global index)
pair the all-gather sends. Today's path launches the bias kernel, the add, torch.max (12.5 us on GB10 at 5 rows) and
the pair's stacking (~6 launches); the Oct 21 prose trace has the Markov phase at 0.48 ms a round. Same arithmetic and
rounding points (the bias rounded to the cache's dtype, the add in fp32 rounded to the logits' dtype, ties to the
lowest index as torch.max), so the drafts are the unfused path's bit for bit: acceptance and greedy text cannot move.
On an RTX 5090 (graph replay, 5 rows): 20.6 -> 16.9 us with every row cached, 32.5 -> 25.9 us with one uncached row.
Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_markov_fused.py (serve image, GPU: 19 cases bit-equal to the unfused path, incl.
forced ties and graph replay; also run on an RTX 5090 against a stand-in vllm package).

